          <a class="amp-link" href="/">← Site</a>
        </div>
        <h1>Mr. Phil</h1>
        <p class="amp-tagline">Your Technology teacher. Code. Games. Video. Media arts.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="amp-grid">
        <section class="amp-panel amp-panel--hero">
          <h2>👋 Hey — you belong here.</h2>
          <p>
            I'm <strong>Mr. Phil</strong>. I teach Tech at DaVinci Academy.
            You matter. This room is safe to ask questions, get stuff wrong, and try again.
          </p>
          <p class="amp-mini">
            You already bring cool ideas to class. My job? Give you chances to learn — from me,
            from friends, and from the work.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="amp-panel">
          <h2>⚡ Mr. Phil's 4 Rules</h2>
          <ol class="amp-rules">
            <li><strong>We build.</strong> You do the work. I guide.</li>
            <li><strong>Mistakes = clues.</strong> Not game over.</li>
            <li><strong>Ball = mic.</strong> Whoever holds the D20 talks. We listen.</li>
            <li><strong>Don't be a Gort.</strong> Ask why. Think for yourself.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="amp-panel">
          <h2>🎮 Class vibes</h2>
          <ul class="amp-chips">
            <li>Hands-on projects</li>
            <li>Code &amp; debug</li>
            <li>Game design</li>
            <li>Video &amp; media</li>
            <li>Free Choice time</li>
            <li>D&amp;D club</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="amp-mini">
            Done with the main task? <strong>Free Choice time</strong> — read, play, catch up,
            or keep building. Freedom <em>and</em> choice. Trust, not chaos.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="amp-panel amp-panel--words">
          <h2>📚 Word Power <span class="amp-sub">(fancy words, plain English)</span></h2>
          <dl class="amp-words">
            <div>
              <dt>Abstraction</dt>
              <dd>Keep the main idea. Drop what doesn't matter. (Stick figure = person. Computer = 1s and 0s.)</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Agency</dt>
              <dd>You get real choices — not just "do what I say."</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Iterate</dt>
              <dd>Try → fix → try again. That's how pros do it.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>

      <footer class="amp-sign">
        <p class="amp-quote">"I want you to see me as a teammate in your joy — not a brick in the wall."</p>
        <p class="amp-outro">Show up. Take a risk. Ask for help. Let's build something awesome.</p>
        <p class="amp-sig">— Mr. Phil</p>
      </footer>
